And what, permitted. Poet, doubt yourself;
But never doubt that you’re a poet to me

peru:
You drifted your dominions
A different Peru;
And I esteemed all poverty,

perchance:
Too cool his temples for the laurel's glow;
But later o'er those marble brows, perchance,
A rose-garden with bushes tall will grow,

perseverance:
Keep a-pluggin' away.
Perseverance still is king;
Time its sure reward will bring;

peril:
And, as the storm drives from the storm, our heart
Within the peril disimperilled grows;
A port is near the more from port we part—

perquisite:
Its other realm of sea;
Without the sterile perquisite
No Caspian could be.

pertaters:
